Half-format conversions under each rounding direction, GCC 14 references,
2026-10-21.
Probe: tests/fixtures/rules-20261013/l03-half-fenv.c
Probe SHA-256: 93f28ac44c3ea843d7334c2c7099c6812fc1277de3479458fed48e77b290be05
Image: evo-nexlab:sealed, linux/arm64, network none, digest
sha256:e8d52bdced1fa49a5a56cde7e1173c54bd81832cc111441f6a31148ec03ead93.
Compiler: gcc-14 (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0.

Command, for LEVEL in -O0 and -O2 and KIND in 0 and 2:
  gcc-14 -std=gnu11 LEVEL -w -frounding-math -ffp-contract=off -DKIND=KIND
         l03-half-fenv.c -o t -lm && ./t

Both levels print the same lines. Each record is KIND=k and one printed
line: the rounding direction, the binary32 input, the half result and the
glibc FE_* flags (invalid 1, overflow 4, underflow 8, inexact 16). Clang 19
and Apple clang give these lines for KIND=0. For KIND=2 they differ in 16
lines: their bfloat16 conversion rounds to nearest in every direction and
raises no inexact, overflow or underflow flag. The machine-read lines
follow the marker.

